Dafny now builds against Boogie v3.5.5+review.dcd726f6, which adds two opt-in options: `--boogie /cacheBackground` restarts a prover's context for a split with the same declarations, seed, type encoding types and SMT options as the context it holds, instead of setting it up again, and sends each solver the same commands, so verdicts and resource counts do not change; `--boogie /scheduleByImplementation` lets an implementation's splits run one after the other on one prover, so that more contexts are restarted, and can change resource counts; a program that uses `--standard-libraries` cannot pass them yet, and by default verification is unchanged
